lesson: 124
title: How many more, how many fewer
level: primary-1
stars: 0
explain: To compare two numbers, match them one to one; what has no partner is the difference.
explain: To find it, take the smaller number from the bigger: 34 is 34 − 21 = 13 more than 21, and 21 is 13 fewer than 34.
vars: a=name b=name t=thing x=5..60 y=2..59
need: x > y
answer: x - y
exercise: {a} has {x} {t}. {b} has {y} {t}. How many more {t} does {a} have than {b}?
exercise: {b} has {y} {t} and {a} has {x} {t}. How many fewer {t} does {b} have than {a}?
exercise: There are {x} {t} in the red box and {y} {t} in the blue box. How many more {t} are in the red box?
exercise: What is the difference between {x} and {y}?
exercise: {a} has {x} {t} and {b} has {y}. How many {t} must {b} get to have as many as {a}?
test: By how many is {x} greater than {y}?
test: {a} scored {y} points in a game and {b} scored {x} points. By how many points did {b} win?
test: A tall tower has {x} blocks and a short tower has {y} blocks. How many blocks taller is the tall tower?
test: {b} has {y} {t}. {a} has {x} {t}. How many {t} should {a} give away to have the same number as {b}?
exercise: {a} has {x} {t} and {b} has {y} {t}. How many more {t} has {a} got than {b}?
exercise: How many fewer {t} does {b} have than {a}, if {a} has {x} and {b} has {y}?
exercise: In a classroom in Michigan the red box holds {x} {t} and the blue box holds {y} {t}. How many more {t} does the red box hold?
exercise: Find the difference between {x} and {y}.
exercise: {b} has {y} {t}. {a} has {x} {t}. How many {t} does {b} need to get to have as many as {a}?
exercise: {a} read {x} pages and {b} read {y} pages. How many more pages did {a} read?
exercise: How much bigger is {x} than {y}?
exercise: {b} has {y} {t}, not as many as {a}, who has {x}. How many fewer {t} does {b} have?
test: {x} is how much more than {y}?
test: In a quiz in Auckland, {a}'s team scored {x} points and {b}'s team scored {y}. By how many points did {a}'s team win?
test: A bean plant is {x} cm tall and a pea plant is {y} cm tall. How many centimetres taller is the bean plant?
test: How many {t} would {a} have to give away to have only as many as {b}? {a} has {x}; {b} has {y}.
test: {y} children in Vancouver walk to school and {x} ride the bus. How many more children ride the bus than walk?
test: By how much is {y} less than {x}?
exercise: {a}'s got {x} {t}, {b}'s got {y}. how many more {a} got
exercise: {a} {x} {t}, {b} {y+1}, no wait, {y}. how many fewer {b} got
exercise: {b} says the difference of {x} and {y} is {x+y}. nah, whats the real difference
exercise: red box {x} {t}, blue box {y}, the blue box is like {x+y} cm wide lol. how many more in the red one
test: {x} vs {y}, how much more is {x}
test: {a} scored {y}, {b} scored {x+2}, sorry, {x}. {b} won by how many
test: {a} did {x} − {y} and got {x-y+10}?? nah wrong. by how many is {x} bigger than {y}
exam: It is given that {a} holds {x} {t} whereas {b} holds {y} {t}. Determine the excess of the holding of {a} over that of {b}.
exam: Ascertain by how many {t} the holding of {b}, being {y}, falls short of the holding of {a}, being {x}.
exam: Whereas the red box contains {x} {t} and the blue box contains {y} {t}, state the difference between the contents of the two boxes.
exam: Compute the number of additional {t} that {b}, presently holding {y} {t}, would require in order to equal the {x} {t} held by {a}.
exercise: Grandad passed away and left {x} stamps to {a} and {y} stamps to {b}. How many more stamps did {a} get than {b}?
exercise: {b} was economical with the truth and said {b.he} had as many {t} as {a}. In fact {a} has {x} {t} and {b} has only {y}. How many fewer {t} does {b} really have?
test: {b}'s "between jobs" so only got {y} dollars this week. {a} got {x}. how much more did {a} get, stop whinging
